---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Workshop - Rumoca"
  description="Hands-On with Rumoca: From Modelica Source to Simulation and Multiple Algebraic Backends in VS Code. A tutorial at the American Modelica & FMI Conference 2026 in Atlanta, Georgia."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20">
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent mb-4">
      American Modelica &amp; FMI Conference 2026 &middot; Workshop
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-text mb-6 leading-tight">
      Hands-On with Rumoca: From Modelica Source to Simulation and Multiple Algebraic Backends in VS&nbsp;Code
    </h1>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-3 text-text-muted mb-12">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-teal shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z" />
        </svg>
        <span>Monday, October 12, 2026 &middot; 10:00 AM &ndash; 1:00 PM</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-teal shrink-0" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M17.657 16.657L13.414 20.9a2 2 0 01-2.827 0l-4.244-4.243a8 8 0 1111.314 0z" />
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M15 11a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z" />
        </svg>
        <span>Georgia Tech, Atlanta, Georgia</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-6 mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text">About the Workshop</h2>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        This tutorial is a hands-on introduction to <span class="text-text font-medium">Rumoca</span>, a Rust-native Modelica compiler that turns a single Modelica model into a universal algebraic frontend for downstream tools.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Working through a set of pre-vetted example models, attendees will use the Rumoca VS Code extension to edit a model, run it, and view the simulation directly in the editor, with live diagnostics and an editable 3D view of the running model. From the same source, participants will then generate exports across several backends, including CasADi, SymPy, JAX, and FMI. These artifacts will then be loaded in their own environment, for example a Jupyter notebook, to inspect them and demonstrate utility.
      </p>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
        No prior Rumoca experience needed; basic Modelica familiarity is helpful, but not required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-6 mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Conference Information</h2>
      <a
        href="https://modelica.org/events/american2026/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-accent text-white font-medium hover:bg-accent-hover transition-colors"
      >
        Conference Page &amp; Registration &rarr;
      </a>
      <p class="text-text-muted leading-relaxed italic">
        Workshop materials will be added at a later date.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-text">Questions?</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-text-muted">
        <li>
          Rumoca on GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/CogniPilot/rumoca" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-teal hover:text-accent underline">github.com/CogniPilot/rumoca</a>
        </li>
        <li>
          Contact: <a href="mailto:condiem@purdue.edu" class="text-teal hover:text-accent underline">condiem@purdue.edu</a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
